  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39471564",
      "title": "Exercise: Interactive Students Administration",
      "lectureOrder": 508,
      "videoOrder": 462,
      "sourceHash": "7c98f0213d8526e1dbfd4bf2bf39f07bbc71faaa9717df0109923cbd0e0ecad9",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "In this lecture, I want to give you a quick exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "And the exercise is to write an interactive bash script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "So the idea here is that we now want to start using those dialogs to allow for easy entry of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.18,
          "end": 20.34,
          "en": "The idea is that we create a bash script to collect student information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 20.34,
          "end": 24.99,
          "en": "Let's say we have an online course and we want to collect all the student information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 24.99,
          "end": 30.93,
          "en": "We can then ask for the name of our students that we want to enroll through dialogue, dash, dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 30.93,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "input box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 39.65,
          "en": "And after this, we want to write this name into a text file to just store all this information there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 39.66,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "After that, we want to be asked whether we want to continue with entering the next name or whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 47.55,
          "en": "we want to quit the program.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 50.82,
          "en": "And then we either continue, of course, or we quit this program.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 50.82,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "So this is just a simple data entry program, but it allows us to practice those dialogues a little",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 57.45,
          "en": "bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 57.45,
          "end": 66.82,
          "en": "And it will also allow us to further investigate how we can turn those dialogues into interactive or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 66.82,
          "end": 70.75,
          "en": "how we can build those dialogues into interactive Bash Scripts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 70.75,
          "end": 74.02,
          "en": "So the finished program could then look something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 74.02,
          "end": 76.12,
          "en": "This is my sample solution here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 76.12,
          "end": 82.63,
          "en": "People can enter the name, so I could just provide a name here, then confirm this with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 82.63,
          "end": 83.08,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 83.11,
          "end": 85.42,
          "en": "Then I'm asked whether I want to continue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 85.42,
          "end": 87.07,
          "en": "I could select yes or no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 87.1,
          "end": 88.53999999999999,
          "en": "Then I can select yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 88.53999999999999,
          "end": 93.75999999999999,
          "en": "Then I could either enter the next name or I could cancel my whole program here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 93.75999999999999,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "Or if I enter a name, I will now just enter another name, Kamelia.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 100.06,
          "end": 102.13,
          "en": "And I will confirm this with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 102.13,
          "end": 102.72999999999999,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 102.72999999999999,
          "end": 108.07,
          "en": "And now if I'm asked if I want to continue, I could then also just select no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 108.07,
          "end": 109.9,
          "en": "And now my script is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 109.9,
          "end": 116.74000000000001,
          "en": "If I now look at the students that have been written, we can see that a text file has been created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 116.74000000000001,
          "end": 117.07,
          "en": "here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 117.07,
          "end": 122.98,
          "en": "In my case it's called Students Dot txt and there we can see those names that I entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 123.01,
          "end": 124.63,
          "en": "They are being written here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 125.17,
          "end": 132.88,
          "en": "This is thus a great example how those dialogue works and it will allow you to later write your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 132.88,
          "end": 135.69,
          "en": "dialogue flows as a simple bash script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 135.7,
          "end": 141.28,
          "en": "So I would advise you, or I would suggest that you can treat this as an exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 141.28,
          "end": 145.78,
          "en": "And then in the next lecture we will have a look at the sample solution for this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
